<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.1.13.2.1"/>
    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Flashes of light and a new floater in the right eye since last evening. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Nietzsche asked for a same-day visit because last evening he began to see brief arcs of light at the outer edge of the right eye&apos;s vision when he moved his eyes, most noticeable in dim light, and this morning a cobweb-like floater that drifts when he looks around. There is no shadow or curtain, no loss of vision beyond his usual poor right eye, and no pain. He has no headache with it, and it is unlike his migraine attacks, which have never had a visual aura. He is in the third week of the butalbital taper, taking one tablet every other day, and had his first galcanezumab injection two weeks ago. He has had no injury to the eye. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Last evening</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Right eye only, outer field</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Flashes of a second or less, repeatedly, since last evening; floater since this morning</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Arcs of light with eye movement; a cobweb-like floater</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Not painful; alarming to him</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>With eye movement, worse in dim light</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>High myopia; poor right eye; third week of the taper</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Not affected by covering the left eye</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No headache, curtain, shadow, pain or injury</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

