    <code code="10160-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Medication use Narrative"/>
    <title>Medications</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Medication</th><th>Frequency</th><th>Route</th><th>Dates</th><th>Status</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr ID="medication-1"><td>Butalbital 50 mg, acetaminophen 325 mg and caffeine 40 mg oral tablet, one or two tablets as needed for headache, taken on about 16 days a month, up to four tablets a day (prescribed abroad)</td><td>One or two tablets as needed, about 16 days a month, up to four a day</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1880-11-03 to 1881-07-21</td><td>stopped</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-2"><td>Ibuprofen 200 mg oral tablet, two tablets as needed for headache on days without the combination tablets, about 4 days a month (over the counter)</td><td>Two tablets as needed, about 4 days a month</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1880-11-03 to 1881-07-21</td><td>stopped</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-3"><td>Butalbital 50 mg, acetaminophen 325 mg and caffeine 40 mg oral tablet, scheduled taper: one tablet twice a day for 7 days, then one tablet a day for 7 days, then one tablet every other day for 7 days, then stop</td><td>Scheduled taper over three weeks: twice a day, then once a day, then every other day, then stop; not for extra doses</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1881-07-21 to 1881-08-10</td><td>completed</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-4"><td>Naproxen 500 mg oral tablet, one tablet with food at the start of a migraine attack, may repeat once after 12 hours; no more than two days a week</td><td>One tablet at attack onset, may repeat once after 12 hours; no more than two days a week</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1881-07-21</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-5"><td>Metoclopramide 10 mg oral tablet, one tablet with the acute medicine when a migraine attack brings nausea or vomiting; no more than two days a week</td><td>One tablet with the acute medicine when nausea is present, no more than once a day</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1881-07-21</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-6"><td>Galcanezumab 120 mg/mL auto-injector, 240 mg (two injections) under the skin as a first loading dose, then 120 mg once a month, for chronic migraine prevention</td><td>Loading dose of 240 mg (two injections) on the first day, then 120 mg every four weeks</td><td>Subcutaneous route</td><td>1881-07-21</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

