    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Frequent disabling headaches on about 20 days a month, with nausea, vomiting and light sensitivity, mostly right-sided, since childhood and more frequent over the past year, with a combination headache tablet containing butalbital taken on about 16 days a month; under evaluation with a headache diary, MRI, syphilis serology and a headache medicine consultation</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R51.9</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented headaches; superseded when the consultation confirmed chronic migraine with medication overuse headache.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Chronic migraine without aura (15 or more headache days a month for more than three months, at least 8 with migraine features); ICHD-3 criteria met in a two-week diary; MRI of the brain normal; synthetic modern diagnosis linked to his documented headaches, which historians interpret differently</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>G43.709</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the consultation; the historical diagnosis is disputed (CLM-0014), so this is not a claim about his real diagnosis.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Medication overuse headache from a butalbital, acetaminophen and caffeine combination on 10 or more days a month for more than three months, with ibuprofen on other days; resolved after a three-week taper and withdrawal</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>G44.40</td><td>S — Synthetic diagnosis made at the consultation, anchored to his documented use of many medicines and sedatives; not a claim about his real medicines.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>High myopia in both eyes, much worse in the right eye, since early childhood, with long-standing poor vision in the right eye and unequal pupils; comprehensive eye examination booked</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>H52.13</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding of his documented severe myopia.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Pathologic (degenerative) myopia of the right eye with patchy chorioretinal atrophy of the macula, a posterior staphyloma and a tilted optic disc; no choroidal neovascularization on OCT; best corrected vision 20/100 in the right eye</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>H44.2E1</td><td>S — Synthetic finding of the comprehensive eye examination, anchored to his documented poor right eye and the retrospective reading of it as myopic degeneration; not a claim about his real eyes.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Chronic insomnia, with difficulty falling asleep and early waking, worse on headache nights; no sleep medicine at intake</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>G47.00</td><td>S — Synthetic sleep problem anchored to his documented severe insomnia; not a claim about his real sleep.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-7">
    <td>Acute posterior vitreous detachment of the right eye, with flashes and a floater, without a retinal break, detachment or vitreous hemorrhage on dilated examination, in an eye with pathologic myopia</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>H43.811</td><td>S — Synthetic acute eye problem in a highly myopic eye; not a historical claim.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

